import Mathlib
import RequestProject.C2Witness

/-!
# The weighted Gross-point class `D_p`, and what the distribution relations do to it

This file carries out one bounded arithmetic derivation.  It takes the weighted class built from
the actual traced conductor-`p²` Gross point `Q₁ = P₁(L) ∈ J ⊗ 𝔽_p`,

    D_p = ∑_{j=0}^{p-1} j² · γ^j Q₁ ,       γ a generator of `G₁ = Gal(K₁/K) ≅ ℤ/p`,

for which the retained identity is `ψ̄_f(D_p) = -2·c̄₂(p)` (`psi_weightedClass_eq_neg_two_mul_c2bar`,
proved here from the layer-one coefficient extraction of `C2Witness`), and computes what the
Gross-point distribution relation and the Hecke action actually do to it.

## 1.  The group-algebra computation

Everything happens inside `Λ₁ ⊗ 𝔽_p = 𝔽_p[G₁] = 𝔽_p[t]/(t^p)`, `t = γ - 1`.  Writing `γ^j = (1+t)^j`
and summing the three weights `1, j, j²` gives *exact* identities in `𝔽_p[t]` (not merely modulo
`t^p`), obtained from `(1+t)^p - 1 = t^p` by differentiating twice:

* `norm_element_eq_X_pow`  : `∑_{j<p} (1+t)^j = t^{p-1}`;
* `weight_one_element`     : `∑_{j<p} j (1+t)^j = -t^{p-2}(1+t)`;
* `weight_two_element`     : `∑_{j<p} j² (1+t)^j = t^{p-3}(1+t)(2+t) = 2t^{p-3}+3t^{p-2}+t^{p-1}`.

So all three weightings of the layer-one Galois orbit land in the *top* three graded pieces of the
augmentation filtration, and (`weightedClass_eq`, `norm_smul_eq`)

    D_p = (1+t)(2+t) · Y ,        N Q₁ = t^{p-1} Q₁ = t² · Y ,        Y := t^{p-3} Q₁ ,

with `N = ∑_{σ∈G₁} σ` the trace (norm) element.  Since `(1+t)(2+t) = 2 + 3t + t²` has unit constant
term `2`, `D_p` is a *unit multiple of `Y`*, while the distribution relation computes `t² Y`.

## 2.  The arithmetic relations, with normalization and conductor indices

BLV's `P_n(L)` is the trace to `K_n` of a special point of conductor `p^{n+1}`; the relation making
`𝓛_{g,n} = α^{-n} ∑_{σ∈G_n}(ψ_g(σP_{n-1}) - α ψ_g(σP_n))σ` norm-coherent is the classical three-term
trace relation between consecutive conductors,

    Tr_{K_n/K_{n-1}} P_n = T_p P_{n-1} - P_{n-2}        (n ≥ 2),
    Tr_{K_1/K}     P_1 = T_p P_0 - c_p P_{-1},   c_p = 2 (p split in K = ℚ(√-7), h(-7)=1),
                                                  c_p = 0 (p inert),

`T_p` the Hecke operator at `p` on `J` (the good-reduction normalization: `p ∤ N`), `ψ_g(T_p x) =
a_p ψ_g(x)`, `α + p/α = a_p`.  Under `ψ̄_f` this is exactly one linear equation on the packet:

    M₀ := ∑_{j<p} ψ̄_f(γ^j Q₁) = a_p ψ̄_f(Q₀) - c_p ψ̄_f(Q_{-1}).

`smul_mul_norm_eq` records the structural point: *closing this relation under the Iwasawa-algebra
action produces nothing new.*  If `γ^p = 1` on `J ⊗ 𝔽_p`, then for every `λ ∈ 𝔽_p[G₁]` one has
`λ · (N Q₁) = ε(λ) · N Q₁`, `ε` the augmentation.  The relation module generated by the
distribution relation is the one-dimensional space `𝔽_p · N Q₁`.

## 3.  The anticyclotomic involution

The second input is `ι : γ ↦ γ^{-1}`.  If the packet is `ι`-even the odd moments vanish — this
re-derives the first-moment vanishing used in the reduction, from the functional equation alone and
independently of the Iwasawa lower-order bound (`momentZ_one_eq_zero_of_even`).  If it is `ι`-odd
then `M₂ = 0` and hence `c̄₂(p) = 0` (`momentZ_two_eq_zero_of_odd`), so `ι`-evenness is a *necessary*
condition for the witness.

## 4.  What the relations leave undetermined

Neither input touches the target.  `exists_even_packet_moments` and `exists_even_packet_c2bar`
exhibit, for every prime `p ≥ 7`, for every value `a` of the trace relation and every prescribed
value of the witness, an `ι`-even packet with `M₀ = a`, `M₁ = 0` realizing it.  The two relations
the arithmetic supplies are therefore compatible with every value of `ψ̄_f(D_p) = -2 c̄₂(p)`.

This is a statement about *this* calculation — one linear equation plus a symmetry, against a
target linear form independent of both — and not an impossibility statement about other methods.
-/

namespace C2Witness

open Finset Polynomial

/-! ## 1. The three weight elements of `𝔽_p[G₁]` -/

section WeightElements

variable (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime]

/-- **The norm element.**  `N = ∑_{j<p} γ^j = t^{p-1}` in `𝔽_p[t]`, `γ = 1 + t`.  (An exact identity
of polynomials, since `(1+t)^p - 1 = t^p` in characteristic `p`.) -/
theorem norm_element_eq_X_pow (hp : 3 ≤ p) :
    ∑ j ∈ range p, ((1 + X : (ZMod p)[X])) ^ j = X ^ (p - 1) := by
  have hx : ((1 + X : (ZMod p)[X])) ^ p - 1 = X ^ p := by
    rw [add_pow_char]; simp
  have h := geom_sum_mul (1 + X : (ZMod p)[X]) p
  simp only [add_sub_cancel_left] at h
  rw [hx] at h
  have hXp : (X : (ZMod p)[X]) ^ p = X ^ (p - 1) * X := by
    rw [← pow_succ]; congr 1; omega
  rw [hXp] at h
  exact mul_right_cancel₀ Polynomial.X_ne_zero h

/-- **The first weight element.**  `∑_{j<p} j·γ^j = -t^{p-2}(1+t)`. -/
theorem weight_one_element (hp : 5 ≤ p) :
    ∑ j ∈ range p, C ((j : ZMod p)) * (1 + X : (ZMod p)[X]) ^ j = -(X ^ (p - 2) * (1 + X)) := by
  have hS := norm_element_eq_X_pow p (by omega)
  have hd : derivative (∑ j ∈ range p, ((1 + X : (ZMod p)[X])) ^ j)
      = ∑ j ∈ range p, C ((j : ZMod p)) * (1 + X) ^ (j - 1) := by
    rw [derivative_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun j _ => ?_)
    rw [derivative_pow]; simp
  have hd2 : derivative ((X : (ZMod p)[X]) ^ (p - 1))
      = C (((p : ℕ) - 1 : ℕ) : ZMod p) * X ^ (p - 2) := by
    rw [derivative_X_pow]; congr 2
  rw [hS, hd2] at hd
  have hcast : (((p : ℕ) - 1 : ℕ) : ZMod p) = -1 := by
    have h : ((p - 1 : ℕ) : ZMod p) = ((p : ℕ) : ZMod p) - 1 := by
      push_cast [Nat.cast_sub (by omega : 1 ≤ p)]; ring
    rw [h]; simp
  rw [hcast] at hd
  have key : (∑ j ∈ range p, C ((j : ZMod p)) * (1 + X) ^ (j - 1)) * (1 + X)
      = ∑ j ∈ range p, C ((j : ZMod p)) * (1 + X : (ZMod p)[X]) ^ j := by
    rw [Finset.sum_mul]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun j _ => ?_)
    rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos j with rfl | hj0
    · simp
    · rw [mul_assoc, ← pow_succ]
      congr 2
      omega
  rw [← key, ← hd]
  simp only [map_neg, map_one]
  ring

/-- **The second weight element.**  `∑_{j<p} j²·γ^j = t^{p-3}(1+t)(2+t) = 2t^{p-3}+3t^{p-2}+t^{p-1}`.
Since `(1+t)(2+t)` has unit constant term `2`, the weighted class `D_p` is a unit multiple of
`t^{p-3} Q₁`: it sits three steps, not one, below the top of the augmentation filtration, whereas
the trace relation reaches only `t^{p-1} Q₁`. -/
theorem weight_two_element (hp : 5 ≤ p) :
    ∑ j ∈ range p, C (((j : ZMod p)) ^ 2) * (1 + X : (ZMod p)[X]) ^ j
      = X ^ (p - 3) * (1 + X) * (2 + X) := by
  have hS1 := weight_one_element p hp
  have hd : derivative (∑ j ∈ range p, C ((j : ZMod p)) * (1 + X : (ZMod p)[X]) ^ j)
      = ∑ j ∈ range p, C (((j : ZMod p)) ^ 2) * (1 + X) ^ (j - 1) := by
    rw [derivative_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun j _ => ?_)
    rw [derivative_C_mul, derivative_pow]
    simp [mul_comm, mul_assoc, mul_left_comm, sq]
  rw [hS1] at hd
  have hXd : derivative (-((X : (ZMod p)[X]) ^ (p - 2) * (1 + X)))
      = -(C (((p : ℕ) - 2 : ℕ) : ZMod p) * X ^ (p - 3) * (1 + X) + X ^ (p - 2)) := by
    rw [derivative_neg, derivative_mul, derivative_X_pow]
    have h : (p - 2 - 1) = p - 3 := by omega
    rw [h]; simp
  rw [hXd] at hd
  have hcast : (((p : ℕ) - 2 : ℕ) : ZMod p) = -2 := by
    have h : ((p - 2 : ℕ) : ZMod p) = ((p : ℕ) : ZMod p) - 2 := by
      push_cast [Nat.cast_sub (by omega : 2 ≤ p)]; ring
    rw [h]; simp
  rw [hcast] at hd
  have key : (∑ j ∈ range p, C (((j : ZMod p)) ^ 2) * (1 + X) ^ (j - 1)) * (1 + X)
      = ∑ j ∈ range p, C (((j : ZMod p)) ^ 2) * (1 + X : (ZMod p)[X]) ^ j := by
    rw [Finset.sum_mul]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun j _ => ?_)
    rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos j with rfl | hj0
    · simp
    · rw [mul_assoc, ← pow_succ]
      congr 2
      omega
  rw [← key, ← hd]
  have hxx : (X : (ZMod p)[X]) ^ (p - 2) = X ^ (p - 3) * X := by
    rw [← pow_succ]; congr 1; omega
  rw [hxx]
  simp only [map_neg, map_ofNat]
  ring

end WeightElements

/-! ## 2. The weighted class `D_p` in `J ⊗ 𝔽_p`, and the distribution relation -/

section GrossModule

variable (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime]
variable {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module (ZMod p) M] [Module (ZMod p)[X] M]
  [IsScalarTower (ZMod p) (ZMod p)[X] M]

/-- `J ⊗ 𝔽_p` is a module over `𝔽_p[G₁] = 𝔽_p[t]/(t^p)`; it is modelled here as a module over
`𝔽_p[t]` on which `t^p` acts by zero (that hypothesis is used only where it is needed, in
`smul_mul_norm_eq`), with `γ = 1 + t`.  The weighted Gross class of the task is

    D_p = ∑_{j=0}^{p-1} j² · γ^j Q₁ . -/
noncomputable def weightedClass (Q : M) : M :=
  ∑ j ∈ range p, ((j : ZMod p) ^ 2) • ((1 + X : (ZMod p)[X]) ^ j • Q)

theorem smul_eq_C_smul (c : ZMod p) (f : (ZMod p)[X]) (m : M) :
    c • (f • m) = (C c * f) • m := by
  rw [← smul_assoc, Polynomial.smul_eq_C_mul]

/-- **The weighted class is a unit multiple of `Y = t^{p-3} Q₁`:**
`D_p = γ(γ+1)·t^{p-3}Q₁ = (1+t)(2+t)·Y`. -/
theorem weightedClass_eq (hp : 5 ≤ p) (Q : M) :
    weightedClass p Q
      = ((1 + X : (ZMod p)[X]) * (2 + X)) • (((X : (ZMod p)[X]) ^ (p - 3)) • Q) := by
  unfold weightedClass
  have h : ∀ j ∈ range p, ((j : ZMod p) ^ 2) • ((1 + X : (ZMod p)[X]) ^ j • Q)
      = (C (((j : ZMod p)) ^ 2) * (1 + X) ^ j) • Q := fun j _ => smul_eq_C_smul p _ _ Q
  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl h, ← Finset.sum_smul, weight_two_element p hp, ← mul_smul]
  congr 1
  ring

omit [Module (ZMod p) M] [IsScalarTower (ZMod p) (ZMod p)[X] M] in
/-- **The trace (norm) element applied to `Q₁`.**  `∑_{σ∈G₁} σ Q₁ = t^{p-1}Q₁ = t²·(t^{p-3}Q₁)`:
the Gross-point distribution relation evaluates the target class only after two further
applications of `t = γ - 1`. -/
theorem norm_smul_eq (hp : 5 ≤ p) (Q : M) :
    ∑ j ∈ range p, ((1 + X : (ZMod p)[X]) ^ j) • Q
      = ((X : (ZMod p)[X]) ^ 2) • (((X : (ZMod p)[X]) ^ (p - 3)) • Q) := by
  rw [← Finset.sum_smul, norm_element_eq_X_pow p (by omega), ← mul_smul, ← pow_add]
  congr 2
  omega

/-- **Closing the distribution relation under the Iwasawa-algebra action gives nothing new.**  If
`γ^p = 1` on `M` (i.e. `t^p` acts by zero) then for every `λ ∈ 𝔽_p[G₁]`

    λ · (N Q₁) = ε(λ) · N Q₁ ,       ε(λ) = λ(0) the augmentation.

So the `𝔽_p[G₁]`-module generated by the single relation `N Q₁ = a_p Q₀ - c_p Q_{-1}` is the
one-dimensional space `𝔽_p · N Q₁`: no `Λ`-multiple of the relation yields a second independent
linear condition on the packet. -/
theorem smul_mul_norm_eq (hp : 3 ≤ p) (hXp : ∀ m : M, ((X : (ZMod p)[X]) ^ p) • m = 0)
    (f : (ZMod p)[X]) (Q : M) :
    (f * X ^ (p - 1)) • Q = (f.coeff 0) • (((X : (ZMod p)[X]) ^ (p - 1)) • Q) := by
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ : (X : (ZMod p)[X]) ∣ (f - C (f.coeff 0)) := by
    rw [Polynomial.X_dvd_iff]; simp
  have hf : f = C (f.coeff 0) + X * g := by linear_combination hg
  have hxp : (X : (ZMod p)[X]) * X ^ (p - 1) = X ^ p := by
    rw [← pow_succ']; congr 1; omega
  rw [smul_eq_C_smul]
  conv_lhs => rw [hf]
  rw [add_mul]
  have h2 : (X * g * X ^ (p - 1)) • Q = (0 : M) := by
    have h3 : (X * g * X ^ (p - 1) : (ZMod p)[X]) = g * X ^ p := by rw [← hxp]; ring
    rw [h3, mul_smul, hXp, smul_zero]
  rw [add_smul, h2, add_zero]

omit [IsScalarTower (ZMod p) (ZMod p)[X] M] in
/-- The value of the eigenfunctional on `D_p` is the second moment of the Gross-point packet
`v j = ψ̄_f(γ^j Q₁)`. -/
theorem psi_weightedClass (ψ : M →ₗ[ZMod p] ZMod p) (Q : M) :
    ψ (weightedClass p Q) = moment p 2 (fun j => ψ (((1 + X : (ZMod p)[X])) ^ j • Q)) := by
  unfold weightedClass moment
  rw [map_sum]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun j _ => by rw [map_smul]; simp [smul_eq_mul])

omit [IsScalarTower (ZMod p) (ZMod p)[X] M] in
/-- **The retained identity, in module form.**  Granting the vanishing of the first moment (either
from the unconditional Iwasawa lower order, or — see `momentZ_one_eq_zero_of_even` — from
`ι`-evenness of the packet),

    ψ̄_f(D_p) = -2 · c̄₂(p). -/
theorem psi_weightedClass_eq_neg_two_mul_c2bar (ψ : M →ₗ[ZMod p] ZMod p) (Q : M)
    (h1 : moment p 1 (fun j => ψ (((1 + X : (ZMod p)[X])) ^ j • Q)) = 0) :
    ψ (weightedClass p Q) = -2 * c2bar p (fun j => ψ (((1 + X : (ZMod p)[X])) ^ j • Q)) := by
  rw [psi_weightedClass]
  have h := two_mul_c2bar p (fun j => ψ (((1 + X : (ZMod p)[X])) ^ j • Q))
  rw [h1, zero_sub] at h
  linear_combination h

end GrossModule

/-! ## 3. The anticyclotomic involution -/

section Involution

variable (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime]

/-- **`ι`-even packets have vanishing first moment.**  The anticyclotomic involution `ι : γ ↦ γ^{-1}`
acts on the packet by `v(-x) = v(x)` when `𝓛^ι = 𝓛`; then `M₁ = 0`.  This re-derives the
first-moment vanishing used in the reduction from the functional equation alone. -/
theorem momentZ_one_eq_zero_of_even (hp : 5 ≤ p) (v : ZMod p → ZMod p) (hv : ∀ x, v (-x) = v x) :
    momentZ p 1 v = 0 := by
  have key : ∑ x : ZMod p, ((-x) ^ 1 * v (-x)) = ∑ x : ZMod p, x ^ 1 * v x :=
    Equiv.sum_comp (Equiv.neg (ZMod p)) (fun y => y ^ 1 * v y)
  have hneg : ∑ x : ZMod p, ((-x) ^ 1 * v (-x)) = -∑ x : ZMod p, x ^ 1 * v x := by
    rw [← Finset.sum_neg_distrib]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun x _ => by rw [hv]; ring)
  have h2 : (2 : ZMod p) * momentZ p 1 v = 0 := by
    unfold momentZ; linear_combination hneg - key
  exact (mul_eq_zero.1 h2).resolve_left (two_ne_zero_of_ne_two p (by omega))

/-- **An `ι`-odd packet kills the witness.**  If `𝓛^ι = -𝓛`, i.e. `v(-x) = -v(x)`, then the second
moment vanishes, hence `c̄₂(p) = 0`.  So `ι`-evenness of the packet is a *necessary* condition for
`c₂(p) ∈ ℤ_p^×`; this is the finite-layer shadow of the fact that `𝓛^ι = -𝓛` forces `2c₂ = 0`. -/
theorem momentZ_two_eq_zero_of_odd (hp : 5 ≤ p) (v : ZMod p → ZMod p) (hv : ∀ x, v (-x) = -v x) :
    momentZ p 2 v = 0 := by
  have key : ∑ x : ZMod p, ((-x) ^ 2 * v (-x)) = ∑ x : ZMod p, x ^ 2 * v x :=
    Equiv.sum_comp (Equiv.neg (ZMod p)) (fun y => y ^ 2 * v y)
  have hneg : ∑ x : ZMod p, ((-x) ^ 2 * v (-x)) = -∑ x : ZMod p, x ^ 2 * v x := by
    rw [← Finset.sum_neg_distrib]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun x _ => by rw [hv]; ring)
  have h2 : (2 : ZMod p) * momentZ p 2 v = 0 := by
    unfold momentZ; linear_combination hneg - key
  exact (mul_eq_zero.1 h2).resolve_left (two_ne_zero_of_ne_two p (by omega))

end Involution

/-! ## 4. What the relations leave undetermined -/

section Undetermined

variable (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime]

omit [Fact p.Prime] in
theorem not_dvd_pred_self (hp : 7 ≤ p) : ¬ (p - 1) ∣ p := by
  intro h
  have h1 : (p - 1) ∣ (p - (p - 1)) := Nat.dvd_sub h dvd_rfl
  have h2 : p - (p - 1) = 1 := by omega
  rw [h2] at h1
  have := Nat.le_of_dvd one_pos h1
  omega

omit [Fact p.Prime] in
theorem not_dvd_two_add_pred (hp : 7 ≤ p) : ¬ (p - 1) ∣ (2 + (p - 1)) := by
  intro h
  have h1 : (p - 1) ∣ ((2 + (p - 1)) - (p - 1)) := Nat.dvd_sub h dvd_rfl
  have h2 : (2 + (p - 1)) - (p - 1) = 2 := by omega
  rw [h2] at h1
  have := Nat.le_of_dvd two_pos h1
  omega

omit [Fact p.Prime] in
theorem not_dvd_of_lt {k : ℕ} (hk0 : 0 < k) (hk : k < p - 1) : ¬ (p - 1) ∣ k :=
  fun h => absurd (Nat.le_of_dvd hk0 h) (by omega)

theorem sum_pow_eq_zero_of_not_dvd {k : ℕ} (hk : 0 < k) (hnd : ¬ (p - 1) ∣ k) :
    ∑ x : ZMod p, x ^ k = 0 := by
  rw [sum_pow_eq_ite p k hk, if_neg hnd]

/-- **The two available relations leave the target completely free.**  For every prime `p ≥ 7` and
every pair `(a, b)`, the explicit packet `v(x) = -a x^{p-1} - b x^{p-3}` is `ι`-even, has zeroth
moment `a` — the value pinned by the Gross-point distribution relation,
`M₀ = a_p ψ̄_f(Q₀) - c_p ψ̄_f(Q_{-1})` — has vanishing first moment, and has second moment `b`.

So the trace relation together with `ι`-evenness and `M₁ = 0` is compatible with every value of
`ψ̄_f(D_p) = M₂`.  This is a statement about these relations, not an impossibility statement about
other methods. -/
theorem exists_even_packet_moments (hp : 7 ≤ p) (a b : ZMod p) :
    ∃ v : ZMod p → ZMod p, (∀ x, v (-x) = v x) ∧ momentZ p 0 v = a ∧ momentZ p 1 v = 0
      ∧ momentZ p 2 v = b := by
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := (Fact.out : p.Prime).odd_of_ne_two (by omega)
  have he1 : Even (p - 1) := ⟨m, by omega⟩
  have he3 : Even (p - 3) := ⟨m - 1, by omega⟩
  refine ⟨fun x => -a * x ^ (p - 1) - b * x ^ (p - 3), ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro x
    have h1 : (-x) ^ (p - 1) = x ^ (p - 1) := by rw [neg_pow, he1.neg_one_pow, one_mul]
    have h3 : (-x) ^ (p - 3) = x ^ (p - 3) := by rw [neg_pow, he3.neg_one_pow, one_mul]
    simp only [h1, h3]
  · unfold momentZ
    simp only [pow_zero, one_mul, Finset.sum_sub_distrib, ← Finset.mul_sum]
    rw [sum_pow_eq_ite p (p - 1) (by omega), if_pos dvd_rfl,
      sum_pow_eq_zero_of_not_dvd p (by omega) (not_dvd_of_lt p (by omega) (by omega))]
    ring
  · unfold momentZ
    have hstep : ∀ x : ZMod p, x ^ 1 * (-a * x ^ (p - 1) - b * x ^ (p - 3))
        = -a * x ^ (1 + (p - 1)) - b * x ^ (1 + (p - 3)) := by
      intro x; rw [pow_add, pow_add]; ring
    rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun x (_ : x ∈ univ) => hstep x)]
    simp only [Finset.sum_sub_distrib, ← Finset.mul_sum]
    have e1 : 1 + (p - 1) = p := by omega
    have e2 : 1 + (p - 3) = p - 2 := by omega
    rw [e1, e2, sum_pow_eq_zero_of_not_dvd p (by omega) (not_dvd_pred_self p hp),
      sum_pow_eq_zero_of_not_dvd p (by omega) (not_dvd_of_lt p (by omega) (by omega))]
    ring
  · unfold momentZ
    have hstep : ∀ x : ZMod p, x ^ 2 * (-a * x ^ (p - 1) - b * x ^ (p - 3))
        = -a * x ^ (2 + (p - 1)) - b * x ^ (2 + (p - 3)) := by
      intro x; rw [pow_add, pow_add]; ring
    rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun x (_ : x ∈ univ) => hstep x)]
    simp only [Finset.sum_sub_distrib, ← Finset.mul_sum]
    have e2 : 2 + (p - 3) = p - 1 := by omega
    rw [e2, sum_pow_eq_ite p (p - 1) (by omega), if_pos dvd_rfl,
      sum_pow_eq_zero_of_not_dvd p (by omega) (not_dvd_two_add_pred p hp)]
    ring

/-- **The witness itself is unconstrained by the relations.**  For `p ≥ 7`, every prescribed value
`c` of `c̄₂(p)` — in particular `c = 0` and every unit — is realised by an `ι`-even packet whose
zeroth moment is the value `a` pinned by the distribution relation and whose first moment vanishes.
-/
theorem exists_even_packet_c2bar (hp : 7 ≤ p) (a c : ZMod p) :
    ∃ v : ZMod p → ZMod p, (∀ x, v (-x) = v x) ∧ momentZ p 0 v = a ∧ momentZ p 1 v = 0
      ∧ c2bar p (fun j => v (j : ZMod p)) = c := by
  obtain ⟨v, hv, h0, h1, h2⟩ := exists_even_packet_moments p hp a (-2 * c)
  refine ⟨v, hv, h0, h1, ?_⟩
  have hm1 : moment p 1 (fun j => v (j : ZMod p)) = 0 := by rw [moment_eq_momentZ]; exact h1
  have hm2 : moment p 2 (fun j => v (j : ZMod p)) = -2 * c := by rw [moment_eq_momentZ]; exact h2
  have h := two_mul_c2bar p (fun j => v (j : ZMod p))
  rw [hm1, hm2, zero_sub] at h
  have h2' : (2 : ZMod p) ≠ 0 := two_ne_zero_of_ne_two p (by omega)
  have : (2 : ZMod p) * c2bar p (fun j => v (j : ZMod p)) = 2 * c := by linear_combination h
  exact mul_left_cancel₀ h2' this

end Undetermined

end C2Witness
